  "presentation_summary": [
    "82-year-old woman with hypertension presented with fever 38.6 degC for four days and mild weakness.",
    "Initial labs showed pancytopenia with WBC 1600/uL, neutrophils 970/uL, hemoglobin 10.7 g/dL, and platelets 85000/uL.",
    "HLH-like labs included ferritin 7146 ng/mL later peaking at 10500 ng/mL, triglycerides 390 mg/dL, LDH 1358 then 1873 U/L, and fibrinogen falling from 134 to 64 mg/dL.",
    "CT did not show splenomegaly or lymphadenopathy, demonstrating that VL-HLH can appear without classic splenomegaly.",
    "Bone marrow showed hemophagocytosis and Leishmania-like parasites; Leishmania antibodies were positive, and liposomal amphotericin B led to fever resolution and recovery."
  ],
